{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqqtne9zs3u","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"agentic abstains on code nodes from rank formula zero boost not model or prompt","summary":"Root cause of multi-round agentic search abstaining on 7/13 code-locator queries (stop_reason insufficient_evidence_quality, selects nothing): a SCORING-CALIBRATION bug, NOT a model or system-prompt issue — there is no LLM and no prompt in the abstention decision (it is the arithmetic check evidence_quality < 0.18 at lib/subconscious/index.js:712). rankResults (lib/subconscious/index.js:886) computes rank_score = score*0.4 + weight*0.12 + tierBoost + (inject?0.25) + lexical*0.35, where the tierBoost map {system:0.18, dag:0.16, dag-note:0.14, surrounding:0.06, rag:0} has NO 'code' entry, so the code tier gets tierBoost 0 and code_nodes also lack the inject(+0.25)/dag/system bonuses. A correct code match therefore lands rank_score about 0.15-0.30 (~ raw cosine * 0.4), straddling the abstention floor SEARCH_CONTEXT_MIN_PROMISING_QUALITY=0.18 and far under the confidence_high bar (needs topQuality ~0.45 since confidence=topQuality*1.6>=0.72). Single-shot /search wins (0.705) because it returns best-effort top-k by raw similarity with NO absolute floor; the enriched embed barely helps agentic because score*0.4 + zero tierBoost still suppresses it under the note-calibrated floor. FIX (no model change): add 'code' to the tierBoost map and/or make the agentic thresholds rank-relative (top-k) instead of absolute floors for the code tier; optionally raise the score coefficient for code. Matters most for MIXED agent-context retrieval (notes plus code in one pass) where code_nodes are unfairly out-competed by notes for selection slots; for a pure recall locator task single-shot already wins at lower cost.","category":"project","tags":[],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-23T15:51:11.879Z","vec":[-0.029562370851635933,0.001486102701164782,-0.03352123871445656,0.009812367148697376,0.06258506327867508,-0.